    "field": "Global vegetation fire modeling",
    "problem": "The original publication of a process-based fire parameterization model contained multiple compensating errors in its equations, data processing, and parameters, which required correction for scientific accuracy even though the final published results were serendipitously unaffected.",
    "method": "This corrigendum corrects compensating errors in a fire parameterization model by revising the ignition efficiency equation, changing a parameter based on corrected fire count data, and doubling the maximum fire spread rate, which coincidentally left the original published results unaffected.",
    "task": "The task is to correct several errors in equations, parameters, and data processing found in a previously published paper on a process-based fire parameterization model, and to show that these errors coincidentally canceled each other out, leaving the original results unaffected.",
